# Implement gate (hard rule)

**No coding** until the operator **explicitly** says **`implement`** in that turn (or a prior turn they have not revoked).

This covers **all** of: Python, JS, HTML, CSS, YAML runtime config, SQL, shell/PowerShell, **`helpers/**` scouts/scripts**, markup that ships with the product, and any other executable or runtime artifact.

## Only keyword that authorizes new code

- **`implement`** — required. Exact word in the operator message (e.g. `implement`, `implement G10`, `implement the discovery helper`).

Also authorize code only when the operator uses these **explicit** ship verbs (same bar — not soft synonyms):

- `ship`
- `patch`
- `fix` / `bugfix` when clearly directed at code (e.g. `patch the door banner`)

If the message does **not** contain one of those words → **do not write or edit code**.

## Does NOT authorize code (non-exhaustive)

- `triage`, `kickoff`, analysis, Q&A, "re-assess", "any open items", "no code"
- Locked spec, kickoff answers, "proposal ok", "this is fine", config shape agreement
- Timing / urgency: **"this is now"**, "do it now", "step 0", "ahead of the bridge", "when ready"
- Scope language: "in this code run", "when you build C31", "roll X into C31", "helper path = …"
- Naming a file (`helpers/foo.py`) or agreeing a scout/script design
- "write the helper" / "create a script" **without** the word **`implement`**
- Pipeline / phase markdown updates during triage or kickoff

**No "helpful" interpretation.** If unsure whether code is allowed → **ask**. Do not start coding.

## Pipeline docs (allowed without `implement`)

- **triage** / **kickoff**: may edit `docs/todo/*` only — **no** product code, **no** `helpers/**`.
- Product docs under `docs/**` outside `todo/` only when the operator explicitly asks for a **docs** change (still no code).
- **implement** / **ship** / **patch**: product code + helpers allowed; pipeline close-out when ship/DoD says so.
- Phase close-out: move Done `docs/todo/phase*.md` → `docs/todo/_archive/` — [`.cursor/rules/phase-archive.mdc`](phase-archive.mdc).

## When unsure

Stop and ask: **triage**, **kickoff**, or **implement**? Do not "helpfully" start coding.

## Conflicts

User Rule **Collaboration standards** wins. This rule makes the implement gate explicit for WanOS: **no code until `implement` (or ship/patch/fix)**.
